{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make _readme_rows slice from the end of the full heading (`start + len(f\"### {section}\")`) instead of `start + len(section)` for clarity/robustness.","criteria":["maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py:154: `start = readme.index(f\"### {section}\")`","tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py:155: `rest = readme[start + len(section) :]`","The offset uses `len(section)` while `start` includes the leading `### ` (4 chars), so `rest` begins inside the heading text; benign today but confusing."],"finding":"_readme_rows slices with `readme[start + len(section):]` but `start` points at the `### ` prefix, so it skips len(section) chars from the `#`, landing 4 chars short of the heading end rather than at the section body. It happens to work only because the row regex matches lines further down; a section whose title text appears again would mis-slice.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py:154","norm_id":"n4ac5229c9628ef62","priority":0.2143,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Use `rest = readme[start + len(f\"### {section}\"):]` so the slice starts cleanly after the heading.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery